{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790360179,"nonce":"EFeOml3VIlWfJAeUL88UlDCXcUw=","message":"Landed 78b4b13 with zyntax 0bd089e4 (zyntax issue 3d13d57a, closed): Lua is embedded as a C host embeds it. zyntax_lua::open_host opens the state with no program run, and zyntax_lua_capi::host_state hands over the main lua_State. A module loads with Lua's own load and runs through zlc_pcall, so an error in its chunk is the load's. The table it returns publishes its functions, each with the parameters its record's arity word names, and a Lua table or function crossing out is a core object (lua.table, lua.function) whose get, set, invoke (receiver first) and call are protected calls of small Lua helpers; it comes back to Lua as itself. tests/lua_module.rs.\n\nThe adapter now runs a module's code (Python's __main__, a Lua chunk) with no borrow of its states held; before, a module importing another language's module would have loaded it under that borrow and panicked.\n\nLeft for the shader from Lua:\n- Haxe imports classes and a Lua module publishes functions, so the gpu fixture's Haxe Main cannot call a Lua module yet. Needs a convention for what of a Lua module is a class.\n- Bytes: writeBuffer and copyOut take a Buffer; Lua's bytes are strings (string.pack/unpack), immutable, so readback needs a Buffer-returning read or strings crossing as buffers.\n- A Lua module required from another Lua module through the world arrives as the world's module, not its table.","files":null}]}